  "notes": {
    "Client/JSON.swift": "→ `client/Json.kt`. `FailableDecodable` is `Json.decodeEach`. The reads bridge numbers and booleans the way `NSNumber` does.",
    "Model/ISOTime.swift": "One ISO parser covers both of LurkerKit's; no lock.",
    "Client/OAuth.swift": "Leaf, but builds `URLRequest`s — waits for the client's request conventions.",
    "Session/SessionStore.swift": "Keychain → interface here, Keystore in `:app`.",
    "Session/OAuthClients.swift": "`UserDefaults` → interface here.",
    "Store/SettingsCache.swift": "`UserDefaults` → interface here.",
    "Client/Uploads.swift": "All but `UploadProgressDelegate` (a `URLSessionTaskDelegate`), which becomes a counting OkHttp `RequestBody` in T6. `assemble` deletes its partial file on failure, which LurkerKit leaves to iOS.",
    "Model/Typing.swift": "`OutgoingTyping` is a mutable class (PORTING.md, structs that mutate, case 3). No Kotlin test until `TypingTests` can run against the store.",
    "Session/NewestAnswer.swift": "A mutable class (case 3).",
    "Model/UploadContentTypes.swift": "`[UTType]` → MIME patterns. Adds `application/json`, which `text/*` cannot reach and `.text` does by conformance.",
    "Model/ServerAddress.swift": "Parses by hand to match `URLComponents`, then also requires that OkHttp can load the address — stricter than iOS at a few edges, pinned by a port-only test.",
    "Model/NetworkAbbreviation.swift": "Grows by code point where Swift grows by grapheme cluster; differs only for names with combining marks.",
    "Commands/SpoilerMarkup.swift": "Checked against the Swift over a corpus; differs only when a combining mark follows a `|`.",
    "Rendering/NickColor.swift": "`lowercase()` applies final-sigma like the web; Swift does not, so a nick ending in `Σ` colours differently on iOS.",
    "Rendering/NickHighlighter.swift": "Case-insensitive matching of non-ASCII nicks is engine-dependent; verify on a device.",
    "Rendering/URLMatcher.swift": "A word boundary beside a combining mark is engine-dependent; verify on a device.",
    "Rendering/IRCFormatting.swift": "`rawIndex` is tested from `RelayEnvelopeTests` (T3); checked against the Swift meanwhile.",
    "Client/NotificationTap.swift": "Input is a `Map<String, Any?>`; FCM's all-strings data map is the shape Android will hand it.",
    "Model/Settings.swift": "`SettingValue.Int` is 32-bit; a wire number past that is skipped rather than wrapped."
  },
